{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.OuterDerivationResidue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.OuterDerivationResidue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.CocenterTraceFactor","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.traceComp_innerDerivation_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.traceComp_innerDerivation_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L85-L95","doc":"**Inner derivations compose to zero with every trace (sorry-free).**  Packaged\nat the level of the functional: `τ ∘ ad_x = 0` as a linear map, for cyclic `τ`.\nA *decision* functional must therefore be sensitive to an **outer** derivation —\nit cannot be a trace (`not_trace_of_separates_commutator`, merged), and the\nderivation it sees cannot be inner. That conjunction — a non-trace functional\ndetecting an outer derivation at the fibre level `H_n(ζ)` — is the precise open\ncontent of `res ≠ 0`. No instance is asserted here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IsInnerDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IsInnerDerivation","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L79-L83","doc":"**`D` is an inner derivation** iff it equals `ad_x` for some `x`.  The\ncomplement — an `R`-linear derivation *not* of this form — is an **outer**\nderivation, i.e. a nonzero class in `HH₁ = Der/Inn`. The decision residue,\nif nonzero, is such an outer class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.trace_comp_innerDerivation_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.trace_comp_innerDerivation_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L67-L75","doc":"**Every inner derivation is trace-blind (sorry-free).**  For a cyclic\nfunctional `τ` (`BilinearTrace.IsCyclic`), `τ (ad_x a) = 0`: the inner part of\n`HH₁` lies in `ker τ = [A,A]`, so it is invisible to the entire magnitude/trace\ntower. This is the `HH₁`-level companion of `trace_eq_of_sub_mem_commutator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerDerivation_leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerDerivation_leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L59-L65","doc":"**`ad_x` is a derivation (Leibniz rule, sorry-free).**  The defining identity\nof `HH₁`'s inner cocycles: `ad_x(a·b) = ad_x(a)·b + a·ad_x(b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerDerivation_mem_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerDerivation_mem_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L52-L57","doc":"**The inner-derivation image lands in `[A,A]` (sorry-free).**  `x·a − a·x` is a\ngenerator of the commutator submodule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerDerivation_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerDerivation_apply","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L48-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.innerDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.innerDerivation","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/OuterDerivationResidue.lean#L43-L46","doc":"The **inner derivation** `ad_x : a ↦ x·a − a·x`, as an `R`-linear map. Built\nfrom `mulLeft x − mulRight x`, so linearity is free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}